# KAIROS — Environment template
#
# Copy this file to one of (uncommitted):
#   .env.development   ← active when APP_ENV=development (default)
#   .env.staging       ← active when APP_ENV=staging
#   .env.production    ← active when APP_ENV=production
#
# Then run:
#   npm run env:dev      → symlinks .env → .env.development
#   npm run env:staging  → symlinks .env → .env.staging
#   npm run env:prod     → symlinks .env → .env.production
#
# Expo inlines any variable prefixed with `EXPO_PUBLIC_` into the JS
# bundle at build time. Restart the dev server after changing the env.
#
# Dev and staging may safely share the same Supabase project (the DEV
# one). Production must point at the prod Supabase. The Groq key in this
# file is DEV-ONLY — production builds use the Supabase Edge Function
# proxy (see supabase/functions/ai-chat) and ship without an LLM key in
# the bundle.

# ── Supabase ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project URL: visible in the dashboard URL.
# Anon key:    Settings → API → Project API keys → "anon / public".
# Safe to expose; Row-Level Security gates access.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Groq (Kai assistant) — DEV ONLY ───────────────────────────────────
# In production, AI calls route through the Supabase Edge Function
# "ai-chat" which holds the real Groq key server-side and gates per-user
# 24h quota. This env var is the legacy fallback used ONLY when there is
# no Supabase session (e.g. SKIP_AUTH=true local development).
#
# Leave EMPTY in builds that ship to TestFlight / App Store — the bundle
# should not contain the production Groq key. If both a session and this
# key exist, the proxy wins.
#
# Enforced: a `APP_ENV=production` build FAILS at config time if this is
# set (app.config.ts), and the app refuses to read it outside a dev build
# (src/lib/ai/devFallback.ts). Two layers so the key cannot ship.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GROQ_API_KEY=
